history of rock music viewed…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":47,"text":"…Blake's visionary symbolism. Neo-classical revival During this era of \"revival\", British musicians mixed rock'n'roll even with classical music. Moody Blues (1) were the prototype for much of Britain's \"symphonic-rock\", \"techno-rock\" and so forth. The mellotron, simulating the stately sound of the…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":59,"text":"…golden age of progressive-rock. The magniloquent, symphonic sound of Ian McDonald's mellotron enrolled them in the neo-classical movement of Nice, Moody Blues and Procol Harum, but the psychedelic overtones, the medieval visions, the gothic atmosphere and the romantic pathos of the title-track and Epitaph…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Early Use of Electronic Drums","body":"Graham Edge of The Moody Blues is noted in historical records for his early use of electronic drums. He collaborated with a professor at Cessax University in this pioneering endeavor. \"As far as history records, the first electronic drums were used by Graham Edge of the Moody Blues when he collaborated with a professor at Cessax University.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"History of the Modern Drum Kit","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WL3zEWJJNuw"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Following Sgt. Pepper's Lead","body":"The Moody Blues were among the bands that got into the act of creating concept albums after the release of The Beatles' *Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band*. \"That opened the floodgates, the moody blues, the who, Frank Zappa, the kinks, and a bunch of other bands got into the act.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alt Rock Concept Albums: Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dm5N6yDRxXQ"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Three Decades of Top 10 American Hits","body":"The Moody Blues achieved the rare distinction of having three Top 10 American hits in three different decades: \"Go Now\" in the 1960s, \"Nights in White Satin\" in the 1970s, and \"Your Wildest Dreams\" in the 1980s. \"In fact the Moody's owned the rare distinction of three top 10 American hits in three different decades.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Second-Chance Hits Edition Part 2","url":null},{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Second-Chance Hits Edition Part 2","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4ef18e6dd12efb02c42e"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"Rock and Roll Hall of Fame (2018)","body":"Won.","year":2018,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q179191"}]}],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Following Sgt. Pepper's Lead","body":"The Who were among the bands that got into the act of creating concept albums after the release of The Beatles' *Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band*. \"That opened the floodgates, the moody blues, the who, Frank Zappa, the kinks, and a bunch of other bands got into the act.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"The Who","from_id":238884878535259,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alt Rock Concept Albums: Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dm5N6yDRxXQ"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Following Sgt. Pepper's Lead","body":"Frank Zappa was among the bands that got into the act of creating concept albums after the release of The Beatles' *Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band*. \"That opened the floodgates, the moody blues, the who, Frank Zappa, the kinks, and a bunch of other bands got into the act.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Frank Zappa","from_id":48325419023266,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alt Rock Concept Albums: Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dm5N6yDRxXQ"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Following Sgt. Pepper's Lead & 70s Golden Age","body":"The Kinks were among the bands that got into the act of creating concept albums after the release of The Beatles' *Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band*, and were also mentioned as a prominent act during the golden age of the concept album in the 1970s. \"That opened the floodgates, the moody blues, the who, Frank Zappa, the kinks, and a bunch of other bands got into the act.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"The Kinks","from_id":115978383810908,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alt Rock Concept Albums: Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dm5N6yDRxXQ"}]}],"charts":[{"id":202509314372117,"type":"song","name":"Go Now","work_year":1965,"list_id":48761518999397,"list":"Billboard Year-End 1965","src":"singles","rank":50,"year":1965,"note":"","yt":"V2L3UzM_FfE","scaruffi":null},{"id":202509314372117,"type":"song","name":"Go Now","work_year":1965,"list_id":132335824845498,"list":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","src":"charts","rank":50,"year":1965,"note":null,"yt":"V2L3UzM_FfE","scaruffi":null},{"id":84813602622166,"type":"album","name":"Go Now: The Moody Blues #1","list_id":107432201760054,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Beat","src":"musthear","rank":92,"year":1965,"note":null,"yt":"KV9W0YJV3Tc","scaruffi":null},{"id":136788223209493,"type":"album","name":"The Magnificent Moodies","list_id":107432201760054,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Beat","src":"musthear","rank":102,"year":1965,"note":null,"yt":"V2L3UzM_FfE","scaruffi":null},{"id":202509314372117,"type":"song","name":"Go Now","work_year":1965,"list_id":58489523060370,"list":"UK nº1 · 1960s","src":"singles","rank":185,"year":1965,"note":"1 semanas","yt":"V2L3UzM_FfE","scaruffi":null},{"id":257870047351289,"type":"album","name":"Days of Future Passed","work_year":1967,"list_id":149374210477972,"list":"AOTY Must Hear 1960s","s